SUMMARY:Career Hour
LOCATION:Tempe - SSV Amphitheater
DESCRIPTION:Join us every Tuesday from 2:00–3:00 PM at the SSV Amphitheat
 er for Career Happy Hour\, a casual drop-in session \ndesigned to help you
  navigate your career journey and connect with helpful resources. During t
 he first 30 minutes\, Career Services staff will \nhighlight career resour
 ces\, job search tools\, upcoming opportunities\, and practical tips for s
 tudent success. The second half of the session is \ndedicated to open Q&A\
 , where you can ask questions about resumes\, job searches\, networking\, 
 internships\, career planning\, and more. \nWhether you're just getting st
 arted or actively searching for opportunities\, Career Happy Hour is a gre
 at place to learn\, ask questions\, and \nget personalized support in a re
 laxed setting. No registration required—just stop by and join the conver
 sation!\n\nRegister: https://career-asu.12twenty.com/events/30006101374499
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gci-fall2026-6-80c1c043@asu-gci-events
DTSTAMP:20260812T191450Z
DTSTART:20260828T190000Z
DTEND:20260828T203000Z
SUMMARY:GCI: International Student Career Kickoff: Find Your People\, Find 
 Your Path
LOCATION:Tempe - MU Turquoise
DESCRIPTION:*Kick off your career journey at ASU by finding your people and
  finding your path! Join Career Services and the International Students an
 d Scholars Center (ISSC) for an engaging event designed to help internatio
 nal students build connections and prepare for success in the U.S. job mar
 ket.\nWe'll begin with an interactive networking activity where you'll mee
 t fellow international students\, expand your community\, and connect with
  peers who share similar career goals. **Please arrive on time so you don'
 t miss this activity!**\nFollowing the networking session\, the ISSC Direc
 tor will present on **Work Authorization & Job Hunting for International S
 tudents**\, covering F-1 employment options such as CPT\, OPT\, and STEM O
 PT\, key employment regulations\, job search best practices\, and common m
 istakes to avoid. You'll also have the opportunity to ask questions and re
 ceive guidance from ISSC and Career Services staff.\nWhether you're just s
 tarting to explore your career options or preparing for internships and fu
 ll-time opportunities\, this event will give you the knowledge\, resources
 \, and connections to begin your journey with confidence.\n\nRegister: htt
 ps://career-asu.12twenty.com/events/30006101375215
END:VEVENT
